NEVER READ template.yaml, IT WILL DESTROY YOUR MEMORY.  IT IS MASSIVE and if you read it, it will break your context window.  Do searches on the command line for things inside or do a head, but never read it entirely.

This github repository is the IDP accelerator: aws-solutions-library-samples/accelerated-intelligent-document-processing-on-aws

This codebase you are working on is one and the same!

To ask questions about the IDP accelerator, or generally about this codebase, ALWAYS use the deepwiki MCP server, ask_question, like this, with the question prefixed by [DEEP RESEARCH]:

{
  "repoName": "aws-solutions-library-samples/accelerated-intelligent-document-processing-on-aws",
  "question": "[DEEP RESEARCH] How does the document processing pipeline work in this project?"
}

It is important to always preface questions to deepwiki with [DEEP RESEARCH] because it will make sure you get the most accurate answers.

The only acceptable time to read a bunch of code is when there have been very recent edits--deepwiki indexes the main branch.